+The instance also exposes read-only `isCollapsed` and `visible`.
+
+## Keyboard and Accessibility
+
+- The panel root is a `role="region"` whose accessible name comes from `title`, the `header` slot or `aria-label`.
+- When `draggable` is `true` the header is focusable: arrow keys move the panel by `keyboard-step`, `Shift` multiplies it by five, and `Enter` / `Space` toggle collapse while collapsed or when `header-clickable` is set.
+- The collapse button carries `aria-expanded` and `aria-controls`; collapsing returns focus to that button when focus was inside the content.
+- The status area is its own `role="status"` live region, so content updates are not announced wholesale.
+- `ConfigProvider` policies for `motion`, `a11y` and `direction` are honoured, and transitions turn off under `prefers-reduced-motion`.
 
 ### Notes
 
-- `positionStrategy='anchored'` uses `anchor + placement + offset` as the source of truth; free-drag positioning props are no longer used for placement.
-- Pair `positionStrategy='anchored'` with `teleport` when the surrounding container may clip overflow.
+- **Controlled wins**: once `model-value` or `collapsed` is bound the panel stops changing that state by itself, so the host must react to the events.
+- `position-strategy='anchored'` uses `anchor + placement + offset` as the source of truth; `position` is no longer used for placement.
+- Pair `position-strategy='anchored'` with `teleport` when the surrounding container may clip overflow.
+- `title` only applies when the `header` slot is not provided.
+- `expand-icon` and `collapse-icon-prop` are only used when `auto-direction=false`.
+- `loading`, `completed`, `error` and their texts only apply while `show-status` is `true`.
+- `resizable` and `show-close` only render while the panel is expanded.
+- The content area scrolls on its own beyond `size.maxHeight`, so the slot does not need another scroll container.
