-# Grid List Auto Height
+# Fill Layout
 
-The Grid List component provides intelligent automatic height calculation functionality that can automatically adjust the height of components and tables based on the actual available space on the page, ensuring a good display experience across different screen sizes.
+Lists, trees and editors often need to "take the remaining height and scroll inside". ZXUI does this with a **pure CSS layout contract**: nothing is measured, nothing observes resizes, no per-page offsets — the browser settles it in one layout pass.
 
-## How It Works
+## Contract
 
-Grid List's automatic height calculation includes two levels:
+| Attribute               | Role                                                                                                                 |
+| ----------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `data-zx-fill-root`     | A region with a **definite height** (the app content area, a fixed-height dialog body…). It offers its height to descendants through container query units. |
+| `data-zx-fill="anchor"` | The page root. Takes the root's full height (`100cqh`) **without depending on** the router-view / transition wrappers in between. |
+| `data-zx-fill`          | One link of the chain: a flex column with `flex: 1 1 0` and `min-height: 0`.                                        |
 
-### 1. Page Layout Height Calculation
+ZXUI components carry these attributes themselves in `fill` mode: `ZxContentWrap fill` is the anchor; `ZxTabs fill`, the `ZxSplitBox` panes and `ZxGridList fill` are links. The host app marks its content region once:
 
-When the component contains specific classes (`zx-grid-list--page`, `grid-list--page`, or `is-page`), it automatically calculates the height the entire component should occupy.
-
-```vue
-<zx-grid-list class="is-page">
-  <!-- Component content -->
-</zx-grid-list>
-```
-
-**Calculation Formula:**
-
-```
-Available Height = Viewport Height - Distance from Top - Bottom Reserved Space
+```html
+<main data-zx-fill-root>
+  <router-view />
+</main>
 ```
 
-Where:
+The host keeps the root at a definite height (for example `height: calc(100vh - header)`, or a flex child of the shell). Ordinary long pages still scroll inside it; fill pages fill it.
 
-- **Viewport Height**: The inner height of the browser window
-- **Distance from Top**: Automatically measured via `getBoundingClientRect().top`
-- **Bottom Reserved Space**: Includes footer height, content padding, parent bottom padding, etc.
+## One list, three places
 
-### 2. Table Height Auto-fit
-
-When the `autoFitTableHeight` property is `true`, the table automatically fills the available height of the container:
+`ZxGridList` on a page, inside a detail tab, or inside a dialog is the same component with one extra prop. Its only requirement is a definite-height flex column as parent — and every candidate parent is a ZXUI component.
 
 ```vue
-<zx-grid-list class="is-page" :auto-fit-table-height="true">
-  <template #table="{ grid }">
-    <el-table :data="grid.list">
-      <!-- Table column definitions -->
-    </el-table>
-  </template>
-</zx-grid-list>
-```
-
-## Height Detection Mechanism
-
-### Automatic Detection of Top Content
-
-The component measures its distance from the top of the viewport in real-time using the browser's `getBoundingClientRect()` API. This distance **automatically includes** the height of all content above, without manual configuration.
-
-**Example Scenario:**
-
-```
-┌─────────────────────────┐  ← Viewport Top (0px)
-│   Navigation Bar (60px) │
-├─────────────────────────┤
-│   Breadcrumb (40px)     │
-├─────────────────────────┤
-│   Title Area (50px)     │
-├─────────────────────────┤  ← grid-list component here
-│   <grid-list />         │     Automatically measured top = 150px
-│                         │
-└─────────────────────────┘
-```
-
-The component doesn't need to know what elements are above; it only needs to measure the actual distance from the top.
-
-### Bottom Space Configuration
-
-For fixed bottom elements (like footers), the component provides three configuration methods:
-
-#### Method 1: Global CSS Variables (Recommended)
-
-Define in global styles:
-
-```css
-:root {
-  --app-footer-height: 60px; /* Bottom footer height */
-  --app-content-padding: 20px; /* Content area padding */
-}
-```
-
-#### Method 2: Component Props
-
-Pass offset through properties:
-
-```vue
-<zx-grid-list class="is-page" :page-viewport-offset="{ top: 10, bottom: 20 }" />
-```
-
-- `top`: Additional top offset (rarely used)
-- `bottom`: Bottom reserved space
-
-#### Method 3: Component-level CSS Variables
-
-Set for specific components:
-
-```css
-.my-grid-list {
-  --zx-grid-list-page-offset-top: 10px;
-  --zx-grid-list-page-offset-bottom: 20px;
-}
-```
-
-## Trigger Timing
-
-Automatic height calculation is triggered in the following situations:
-
-1. **On Component Mount** - Initialize layout
-2. **On Window Resize** - Responsive adjustment
-3. **On Container Size Change** - Monitor via `ResizeObserver`
-4. **On Property Change** - Such as `autoFitTableHeight`, `pageViewportOffset`, etc.
-
-## Common Issues
-
-### Excessive Bottom Whitespace
-
-If you find the bottom reserved space is too large, troubleshoot as follows:
-
-#### 1. Check Global CSS Variables
-
-Execute in browser console:
-
-```javascript
-getComputedStyle(document.documentElement).getPropertyValue(
-  '--app-footer-height'
-)
-getComputedStyle(document.documentElement).getPropertyValue(
-  '--app-content-padding'
-)
-```
-
-#### 2. Check Component CSS Variables
-
-```javascript
-const gridEl = document.querySelector('.zx-grid-list-wrapper')
-getComputedStyle(gridEl).getPropertyValue('--zx-grid-list-page-offset-bottom')
-```
+<!-- page level -->
+<ZxContentWrap title="Users" fill>
+  <ZxGridList :load-data="load" fill>…</ZxGridList>
+</ZxContentWrap>
 
-#### 3. Check Parent Element and Self Styles
+<!-- inside a detail tab -->
+<ZxContentWrap fill>
+  <ZxTabs :items="tabs" fill />
+  <!-- tab component: <ZxGridList :load-data="load" fill /> -->
+</ZxContentWrap>
 
-```javascript
-const gridEl = document.querySelector('.zx-grid-list-wrapper')
-getComputedStyle(gridEl.parentElement).paddingBottom // Parent bottom padding
-getComputedStyle(gridEl).marginBottom // Component bottom margin
+<!-- ordinary flow: no fill, content height, the page scrolls -->
+<ZxGridList :load-data="load" />
 ```
 
-#### Solutions
-
-**Solution 1: Override CSS Variables**
-
-```css
-:root {
-  --app-footer-height: 0px;
-  --app-content-padding: 0px;
-}
-```
-
-**Solution 2: Adjust Props**
-
-```vue
-<zx-grid-list class="is-page" :page-viewport-offset="{ bottom: 0 }" />
-```
-
-**Solution 3: Remove Parent Element Padding**
-
-```css
-.grid-list-container {
-  padding-bottom: 0 !important;
-}
-```
-
-### Inaccurate Height Calculation
-
-Ensure the following conditions are met:
-
-1. Component has `is-page` or related class added
-2. Component is properly rendered in the DOM
-3. Parent container doesn't have styles like `display: none` that affect measurement
-
-### Disable Auto Height
-
-If you don't need the auto height feature:
-
-```vue
-<!-- Don't add page-related class -->
-<zx-grid-list>
-  <!-- Component will use 100% height relative to parent container -->
-</zx-grid-list>
-```
-
-Or set a fixed height:
-
-```css
-.my-grid-list {
-  height: 600px !important;
-}
-```
-
-## Best Practices
-
-### 1. Full-page List Scenario
-
-```vue
-<template>
-  <div class="page-container">
-    <zx-grid-list
-      class="is-page"
-      :auto-fit-table-height="true"
-      :request="loadData"
-    >
-      <template #table="{ grid }">
-        <el-table :data="grid.list">
-          <el-table-column prop="name" label="Name" />
-          <el-table-column prop="value" label="Value" />
-        </el-table>
-      </template>
-    </zx-grid-list>
-  </div>
-</template>
-```
-
-### 2. With Fixed Footer
-
-```css
-/* Global styles */
-:root {
-  --app-footer-height: 60px;
-}
-```
-
-```vue
-<template>
-  <div class="app">
-    <header>Top Navigation</header>
-    <main>
-      <zx-grid-list class="is-page" />
-    </main>
-    <footer style="height: 60px;">Bottom Footer</footer>
-  </div>
-</template>
-```
-
-### 3. Fine-tune Offsets
-
-```vue
-<zx-grid-list
-  class="is-page"
-  :page-viewport-offset="{
-    top: 0, // No additional top offset
-    bottom: 80, // Reserve 80px at bottom (60px footer + 20px margin)
-  }"
-/>
-```
-
-## Technical Details
-
-### Core Implementation
-
-The core logic for automatic height calculation is in the `useGridLayout` composable:
-
-- **`measurePageLayoutHeight`** - Measure and set page layout height
-- **`applyAutoTableHeight`** - Apply table auto-fit height
-- **`setupAutoHeightTracking`** - Setup automatic height tracking (using ResizeObserver)
-
-### CSS Variables
-
-The component uses the following CSS variables:
-
-- `--zx-grid-list-page-height-local` - Calculated page height (dynamically set by JS)
-- `--zx-grid-list-page-offset-top` - Top offset
-- `--zx-grid-list-page-offset-bottom` - Bottom offset
-- `--app-footer-height` - Global footer height
-- `--app-content-padding` - Global content padding
-
-### Browser Compatibility
+Toolbars, stat cards or alerts above the list need nothing: they are not links and keep their content height.
 
-- `getBoundingClientRect()` - Supported by all modern browsers
-- `ResizeObserver` - Supported by modern browsers, falls back to `window.resize` listener for older browsers
-- `requestAnimationFrame` - Used for performance optimization, executes synchronously when not supported
+## Development diagnostics
 
-## Summary
+A flex height chain fails silently — no error, the table just stops short. In development, a `fill` list walks its ancestors once after mount and names the first one that is not a flex column, has no `min-height: 0`, or does not grow. None of this ships in production bundles.
 
-The Grid List's automatic height calculation feature can adapt to various complex page layout requirements through intelligent measurement and flexible configuration. The core principle is to use browser APIs to measure element positions in real-time, combined with configured bottom reserved space, to calculate the optimal component height.
+## Browsers
 
-For most scenarios, simply adding the `is-page` class and configuring the global footer height is enough to achieve good adaptive effects.
+`100cqh` needs Chrome 105 / Safari 16 / Firefox 110. Older browsers fall back to `height: 100%`, in which case no `height: auto` wrapper may sit between the anchor and the root.
